  </Fragment>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       HERO
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="page-hero" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT MAXIFI DIGITAL</p>
    <h1 id="about-heading" class="page-h1">
      About Maxifi Digital
    </h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      Maxifi Digital is a Singapore-based Answer Engine Optimisation (AEO) consultancy,
      founded by Lim Le-Anne and working globally, that builds AI citation authority for
      expert-led brands. We work with professional services firms, industry associations,
      aviation and aerospace bodies, law firms, and specialist consultancies — organisations
      whose buyers now research vendors in AI tools before they ever visit a website.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       WHY AEO MATTERS
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section section--cream" aria-labelledby="why-heading">
    <p class="s-eyebrow">WHY THIS MATTERS NOW</p>
    <h2 id="why-heading" class="section-h2">Search behaviour is shifting to AI</h2>
    <div class="prose-col prose-wide">
      <p class="prose">
        For twenty years, expert-led brands built authority by ranking on Google. Today, that
        strategy is obsolete. Buyers no longer enter keywords into a search box — they ask questions
        in ChatGPT, Perplexity, Claude, Gemini, or Copilot. When they do, they see synthesised
        answers that cite the sources an AI engine judges most authoritative and structured.
      </p>
      <p class="prose">
        A brand can rank on page one of Google and remain invisible in AI answers. Conversely, a
        brand can have zero search rankings and dominate AI-generated responses — if its content
        is structured for retrieval and its entity signals are clear.
      </p>
      <p class="prose">
        This shift is not theoretical. In B2B buyer research across professional services,
        aviation, law, and consultancy, AI is now the primary discovery channel. Buyers form opinions
        about which vendors to contact based on which brands are cited in AI responses. A brand not
        cited is a brand not considered. Answer Engine Optimisation closes that visibility gap.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       FOUNDER
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="founder-heading">
    <p class="s-eyebrow">OUR FOUNDER</p>
    <h2 id="founder-heading" class="section-h2 founder-name">Lim Le-Anne</h2>
    <p class="founder-title">
      Founder, Maxifi Digital ·
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/limleanne/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="founder-link">LinkedIn</a>
    </p>
    <div class="prose-grid">
      <div class="prose-col">
        <p class="prose">
          Lim Le-Anne founded Maxifi Digital after observing a consistent pattern: expert-led
          brands that had invested years building genuine authority were invisible in
          AI-generated answers — not because their expertise was thin, but because their
          content was not structured for machine comprehension.
        </p>
        <p class="prose">
          Previously, she led visibility strategy for a Singapore-based technology consultancy,
          where she worked with law firms, professional associations, and industry bodies to navigate
          the shift from search engine rankings to AI-driven discovery. She recognised early that
          traditional SEO expertise would not transfer to the AI era: what works for ranking pages
          does not work for being cited in synthesised responses.
        </p>
        <p class="prose">
          She built Maxifi Digital to close that gap. Her work sits at the intersection of
          content strategy, structured data, and the emerging science of how AI engines
          select, attribute, and cite sources in synthesised responses. Every engagement
          is grounded in measurement: citation share before, citation share after.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="values-col">
        <!-- Photo slot: drop the founder photo into /public/founder/le-anne-lim.jpg,
             then replace this placeholder div with:
             <img class="founder-photo" src="/founder/le-anne-lim.jpg"
                  alt="Lim Le-Anne, founder of Maxifi Digital" width="360" height="360" /> -->
        <figure class="founder-photo-slot" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="founder-photo-initials">LL</span>
          <figcaption class="founder-photo-caption">Lim Le-Anne · Founder</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="value-card">
          <h3 class="vc-title">Depth over volume</h3>
          <p class="vc-body">We work with a small number of clients at a time. Deep beats broad every quarter.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="value-card">
          <h3 class="vc-title">Results before rhetoric</h3>
          <p class="vc-body">Every engagement starts with a Snapshot. Every claim is measured against a baseline.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="value-card">
          <h3 class="vc-title">Expert-led, always</h3>
          <p class="vc-body">We structure and amplify the expertise that already exists — we don't generate content for volume.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       PROOF — ASW HUB
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="proof-heading">
    <p class="s-eyebrow">PROOF, NOT PROMISES</p>
    <h2 id="proof-heading" class="section-h2">The ASW hub: from launch to AI citation in 62 days</h2>
    <div class="prose-col prose-wide">
      <p class="prose">
        We test our own method in public. In 2026 we built the
        <a href="https://aswhub.maxifidigital.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="prose-link">Airspace World 2026 AI Visibility Hub</a>
        — a citation-optimised knowledge hub for the aviation industry's flagship air traffic
        management event — and tracked how long it took AI engines to start citing it.
        The answer: 62 days from launch to first citation.
      </p>
      <p class="prose">
        By the July 2026 citation audit, Microsoft Copilot was building its answer to the
        event discovery query directly from hub pages — placing the hub above the official
        event website — and citing a hub insight article inside its AI answer. Perplexity
        was recommending the hub as the "best starting point" for researching the event.
        The hub is live, and every claim can be re-run in the engines today.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="proof-stats">
      <div class="proof-stat">
        <div class="proof-stat__value">62 days</div>
        <div class="proof-stat__label">launch to first AI citation</div>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-stat">
        <div class="proof-stat__value">Copilot</div>
        <div class="proof-stat__label">discovery answer built from hub pages · Jul 2026</div>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-stat">
        <div class="proof-stat__value">Perplexity</div>
        <div class="proof-stat__label">cited the hub as "best starting point" · Jul 2026</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       WHAT WE DO
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section section--cream" aria-labelledby="what-heading">
    <p class="s-eyebrow">WHAT WE DO</p>
    <h2 id="what-heading" class="section-h2">The Visibility Engine</h2>
    <div class="prose-col prose-wide">
      <p class="prose">
        AI engines cannot cite what they cannot read. When a buyer asks ChatGPT, Perplexity,
        or Google AI Overviews which firm to trust in a given category, the engine synthesises
        an answer from sources it can parse, attribute, and verify. Most expert-led brands
        publish content written for humans and ignored by machines — unstructured,
        entity-ambiguous, and invisible to retrieval models. The result: buyers receive
        AI answers that name competitors, not our clients.
      </p>
      <p class="prose">
        Maxifi Digital fixes this through the Visibility Engine: a three-stage programme
        that begins with a scored Snapshot audit across five AI engines, moves into a
        structured Sprint that creates citation-optimised content assets, and concludes
        with ongoing monitoring of citation share as engine behaviour evolves. Every
        asset we build increases the probability that AI engines surface our clients in
        future queries — without additional spend per impression.
      </p>
      <p class="prose">
        This is not content generation. We do not publish for volume. Instead, we work with the
        expertise your organisation already possesses — your team's knowledge, your case studies,
        your thought leadership — and structure it in a way that AI engines can parse, understand,
        and cite with confidence. The result is a compounding asset: each piece of structured
        content reinforces your brand's association with your category, making it increasingly
        likely that future AI responses will surface you by name.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="method-steps">
      <article class="method-step">
        <p class="ms-num">01</p>
        <h3 class="ms-title">Snapshot</h3>
        <p class="ms-body">
          A scored baseline of your current citation footprint across ChatGPT, Perplexity, Claude, Gemini, and Copilot.
          We test real buyer questions in your category and report exactly where you stand vs competitors.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="method-step">
        <p class="ms-num">02</p>
        <h3 class="ms-title">Sprint</h3>
        <p class="ms-body">
          Three to six weeks of structured content development, schema markup, and entity signal improvements.
          We build FAQ pages, entity clarification, structured data, and positioning that close citation gaps.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="method-step">
        <p class="ms-num">03</p>
        <h3 class="ms-title">Monitor</h3>
        <p class="ms-body">
          Monthly tracking across all five engines with quarterly re-Snapshots. We show the citation
          growth you're generating and adapt as engine behaviour evolves.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       WHERE WE WORK
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="where-heading">
    <p class="s-eyebrow">WHERE WE WORK</p>
    <h2 id="where-heading" class="section-h2">Singapore-based. Working globally.</h2>
    <div class="prose-col prose-wide">
      <p class="prose">
        Maxifi Digital is based in Singapore and works with clients globally. Our engagements
        are conducted remotely. Our focus is on industries where expert authority, trust,
        and citation credibility matter — aviation, professional services, law, and specialist
        B2B consultancy.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="client-grid">
      {[
        'Professional associations',
        'Conference and event organisers',
        'Law firms',
        'Management consulting firms',
        'Think tanks',
        'Aviation and aerospace organisations',
        'Finance businesses',
        'Healthcare organisations',
      ].map((name) => (
        <div class="client-pill">{name}</div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       HOW WE WORK
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
    <p class="s-eyebrow">HOW WE WORK</p>
    <h2 id="how-heading" class="section-h2">Our approach</h2>
    <div class="prose-col prose-wide">
      <p class="prose">
        Every AEO engagement rests on four principles:
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="principles-grid">
      <article class="principle-card">
        <h3 class="principle-title">Work with existing expertise</h3>
        <p class="principle-body">
          We do not generate content for content's sake. Instead, we identify the knowledge,
          insights, and authority your team already possesses and structure it so that AI engines
          understand and cite it. This is amplification, not invention.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle-card">
        <h3 class="principle-title">Measurement comes first</h3>
        <p class="principle-body">
          Every engagement starts with a Snapshot baseline. Every recommendation is tested.
          Every success is measured against citation share before and after. We do not make
          claims without data to back them.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle-card">
        <h3 class="principle-title">Long-term over quick wins</h3>
        <p class="principle-body">
          AI citation authority compounds. A brand that appears consistently in AI answers over months
          and quarters builds an association that is increasingly difficult for competitors to displace.
          We optimise for sustained visibility, not short-term spikes.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle-card">
        <h3 class="principle-title">Stay current with engines</h3>
        <p class="principle-body">
          AI engines evolve. Their retrieval logic, weighting algorithms, and citation preferences change
          as new versions release and new engines emerge. We monitor this evolution and adapt your strategy
          to remain effective as the landscape shifts.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       CLIENT OUTCOMES
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section section--cream" aria-labelledby="outcomes-heading">
    <p class="s-eyebrow">CLIENT OUTCOMES</p>
    <h2 id="outcomes-heading" class="section-h2">What improves</h2>
    <div class="prose-col prose-wide">
      <p class="prose">
        When an expert-led brand completes a Visibility Engine Sprint, several things change:
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="outcomes-grid">
      <div class="outcome-item">
        <h3 class="outcome-title">Citation share increases</h3>
        <p class="outcome-body">
          More AI responses surface your brand by name, across more engines, in response to more buyer questions.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="outcome-item">
        <h3 class="outcome-title">Buyer pipeline shifts</h3>
        <p class="outcome-body">
          Inbound inquiries come from buyers who encountered your brand in AI answers. These prospects have higher
          intent and clearer understanding of your expertise.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="outcome-item">
        <h3 class="outcome-title">Authority compounds</h3>
        <p class="outcome-body">
          Each piece of structured content and citation reinforces your brand-category association. Growth accelerates
          over time as AI engines recognise the pattern.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="outcome-item">
        <h3 class="outcome-title">No recurring cost per impression</h3>
        <p class="outcome-body">
          Unlike paid ads that cost money every time someone sees them, structured content and citations compound
          without additional spend. The visibility grows without growing the cost.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       DISAMBIGUATION + FAQ
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <p class="s-eyebrow">COMMON QUESTIONS</p>
    <h2 id="faq-heading" class="section-h2">Frequently asked questions</h2>

